 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nRun.iter_inner_content() incorrectly processes XML elements in a run\n\nDescription\n\nI'm working with python-docx and found an issue with the `Run.iter_inner_content()` method. When a run contains multiple elements like text, line breaks, and rendered page breaks, the method doesn't correctly process them.\n\nFor example, with a run containing text, a line break, a rendered page break, a non-breaking hyphen, and more text, the method should yield three items: a string, a RenderedPageBreak object, and another string. However, it's not correctly handling these elements.\n\nHere's a reproduction case:\n\n```python\nfrom docx import Document\n\n# Create a document with a run containing multiple elements\ndocument = Document()\nparagraph = document.add_paragraph()\nrun = paragraph.add_run()\nrun.add_text(\"abc\")\n# Add a line break, page break, etc.\n# ...\nrun.add_text(\"def\")\n\n# Try to iterate through the inner content\nfor item in run.iter_inner_content():\n    print(type(item).__name__)\n```\n\nExpected output:\n```\nstr\nRenderedPageBreak\nstr\n```\n\nActual output:\nThe method doesn't correctly process the elements and doesn't yield the expected items.\n\nSimilarly, when a run contains text, a rendered page break, and a drawing element, it should yield a string, a RenderedPageBreak object, and a Drawing object, but it fails to do so correctly.\n\nThis issue appears to be related to how the method processes the XML elements in the run. The current implementation doesn't properly handle all the different types of elements that can appear in a run.\n</issue>\n",
